# MicroLink size profile: an overlay for any example's sdkconfig.defaults.
#
#   cd examples/basic_connect
#   idf.py -D SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;../sdkconfig.size.defaults" build
#
# (sdkconfig.credentials, if present, is still added by the example's
# CMakeLists.) sdkconfig defaults only apply when sdkconfig is created, so
# delete the example's sdkconfig when switching profiles.
#
# Measured on esp32s3 (image size, example defaults -> this profile):
#   ESP-IDF 5.3    basic_connect     995,996 -> 769,012 bytes  (-222 KB)
#                  cellular_connect  782,904 -> 598,840 bytes  (-180 KB)
#   ESP-IDF 6.1.1  basic_connect     991,915 -> 855,635 bytes  (-133 KB)
#                  cellular_connect  721,771 -> 639,463 bytes  (-80 KB)
#
# Trade-offs; check them against your deployment before shipping:
# - CA bundle: common CAs only. Let's Encrypt (Tailscale control plane and
#   DERP) is included; a headscale/DERP server whose certificate chains to a
#   less common CA needs the full bundle back.
# - newlib-nano printf/scanf (ESP-IDF 5.x; ESP-IDF 6 uses picolibc): no 64-bit
#   or float conversions. MicroLink's logs avoid them; check your own code.
# - mbedTLS: TLS client only, no renegotiation, fewer curves and ciphers.
#   Tailscale needs ECDHE (P-256/P-384/X25519) with AES-GCM, which stay.
# - mbedTLS ChaCha20-Poly1305 is off: MicroLink's Noise channel uses the
#   wireguard_lwip implementation. TLS then offers AES-GCM suites only.
# - WiFi: no WPA2/WPA3-Enterprise, no SoftAP, no OWE.
# - esp_err_to_name() returns numbers only; logs have no colours.
#
# MicroLink's own INFO logs can go too (another 17-23 KB, but the log then
# only shows warnings and errors):
# CONFIG_ML_LOG_LEVEL_WARN=y

# Certificates
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_CERTIFICATE_BUNDLE_DEFAULT_CMN=y

# C library formatting (newlib only; ESP-IDF 6 defaults to picolibc)
CONFIG_NEWLIB_NANO_FORMAT=y

# mbedTLS: client only, trimmed features
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_TLS_CLIENT_ONLY=y
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_SSL_RENEGOTIATION=n
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_ERROR_STRINGS=n
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_PEM_WRITE_C=n
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_X509_CRL_PARSE_C=n
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_X509_CSR_PARSE_C=n
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_PKCS7_C=n
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_CCM_C=n
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_CMAC_C=n
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_CHACHA20_C=n
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_POLY1305_C=n
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_CHACHAPOLY_C=n
# Static ECDH key exchanges (ECDHE stays)
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_KEY_EXCHANGE_ECDH_ECDSA=n
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_KEY_EXCHANGE_ECDH_RSA=n
# Curves: keep P-256, P-384 and Curve25519
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP192R1_ENABLED=n
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP224R1_ENABLED=n
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP521R1_ENABLED=n
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP192K1_ENABLED=n
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP224K1_ENABLED=n
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP256K1_ENABLED=n
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_BP256R1_ENABLED=n
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_BP384R1_ENABLED=n
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_BP512R1_ENABLED=n

# WiFi station without Enterprise, SoftAP or OWE
CONFIG_ESP_WIFI_ENTERPRISE_SUPPORT=n
CONFIG_ESP_WIFI_SOFTAP_SUPPORT=n
CONFIG_ESP_WIFI_ENABLE_WPA3_OWE_STA=n

# Strings
CONFIG_ESP_ERR_TO_NAME_LOOKUP=n
CONFIG_LOG_COLORS=n
